Kali usually comes with the networking tools we need, but just to be safe,
ensure the scapy library is installed
sudo apt install python3-scapy
Make the tool executable:
Tell Linux that this file is a program that can be run, rather than just text to be read
chmod +x vcapture.py
Move the file into your system's binary folder and drop the .py extension. This is the magic step that lets you type vcapture from anywhere, just like nmap or ls:
sudo mv vcapture.py /usr/local/bin/vcapture
